window.GUIDE_SEARCH = [{"file": "experience.html", "title": "Sensory & motion", "text": "Sensory & service 04 / EXPERIENTIAL IDENTITY Make the pause tangible. Every touchpoint supports a comfortable progression, from the first welcome to something taken home. 01 Arrive Understand the offer. 02 Settle in Feel comfortable. 03 Discover One pairing at a time. 04 Linger Let conversation stay. 05 Take it home Carry the ritual on. SPACE Intimate by design. Small tables, comfortable upholstery, warm indirect light, and visible service. Adapt the footprint for venues, expos or a mobile setup while preserving seated discovery. TOUCH Craft you can feel. Terracotta, ceramic serving pieces, textiles and glass charms make the identity tangible. Prototype weight, attachment, edges and cleaning before production. SOUND Leave room to talk. Italian cinematic jazz and instrumental Piero Piccioni references create a gentle background. Avoid abrupt shifts; keep conversation in the foreground. Listening reference ↗ SCENT Flavors first. Scents after. Keep added fragrance out of the tasting space. Introduce aromatic hand wash afterward, in a separate wash area. A gentle arrival. An easy transition. MOTION & PACING PROPOSED TIMING 0.8s fade in 2.4s readable hold 0.8s fade out Play sequence ↻ Manual playback. The original artwork stays intact. Reduced-motion preferences use a static alternative. INTERACTION Progress through information; never force a wait. Use 200–300ms transitions for interface changes, visible focus states and labels. Keep every control usable by keyboard. INTERACTION EXAMPLE One course at a time. ← Previous Next course → ← PREVIOUS Image direction NEXT → Application library Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "voice.html", "title": "Personality & voice", "text": "Foundations Voice & personality FOUNDATION / PERSONALITY & VOICE The Effortless Host. Thoughtful, warm, unhurried. Guide with small invitations and familiar language. PERSONALITY & VOICE Thoughtful, warm, and unhurried. Everything is planned with intention, while the experience feels easy. Use concise, suggestive, pairing-led language. Invite guests to notice what changes; leave specialist wine vocabulary behind. USE “Try the gelato, then the wine. Notice what changes.” AVOID “Follow these steps for the correct tasting experience.” USE “Stay for another taste.” AVOID “Hurry. Don’t miss the ultimate luxury experience.” Service formats & consistent vocabulary + Four ways to enter Pairing Menu for Two: the signature three-course ritual. Seasonal Menu: three new seasonal courses. Single Pair: a shorter introduction. Zero-Proof Menu: the same structure without alcohol. Words we use Write the name as ’while. Use “gelato,” “pairing,” “Bright Start,” “Soft Middle,” and “Long Finish.” Keep “Coursed Ice Cream Bar” as the category descriptor. Do not invent prices, locations, availability, ingredients or official partnership claims. ← PREVIOUS Brand overview NEXT → Logo & variations Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "colors.html", "title": "Color palette", "text": "Logo Typography Color VISUAL SYSTEM / COLOR Warmth. Space. Structure. Three colors, each with a clear role. Click a swatch to copy its HEX value. CLICK A SWATCH TO COPY Warm Orange #FF9A3E RGB 255 / 154 / 62 ↗ Soft Cream #FDFFEE RGB 253 / 255 / 238 ↗ Deep Charcoal #3D3535 RGB 61 / 53 / 53 ↗ USE WITH CARE Use charcoal on cream or orange for essential text. Orange on cream is approximately 2.08:1 and is unsuitable for essential text. Digital normal text needs 4.5:1 contrast; large text needs 3:1. Proof print colors on the selected stock. ← PREVIOUS Typography NEXT → Patterns & graphics Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "resources.html", "title": "Downloads", "text": "Prompt library Review checklist Downloads 07 / RESOURCES A good place to begin again. Use original files. Keep the reference close. Brand guideline book 80-page reference / PDF ↗ Original wordmark Vector artwork / SVG ↗ Original supporting contour Extracted source path / SVG ↗ Approved logo variations Visual reference sheet / PNG ↗ Complete prompt library Permanent foundation + 10 application modules / TXT ↗ ← PREVIOUS Review checklist NEXT → Overview Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "logos.html", "title": "Logo & variations", "text": "Logo Typography Color 02 / PRIMARY IDENTITY Keep the signature intact. Use the original artwork, a deliberate type pairing, and three recognizable colors. THE ORIGINAL WORDMARK Original artwork. Always. Download SVG ↗ A mark for every context. The horizontal wordmark is the compact signature. Filled and outlined organic versions create a self-contained presence. Use dispersed-letter versions at a scale that preserves legibility. Never retype, stretch, redraw, rearrange, or add effects to the logo. Approved variants from the original brand artwork. Clear space, size testing & co-branding + Give it space. Proposed: use the apostrophe height as x around the horizontal wordmark; use ¼ of the shape height for organic versions. Confirm against master artwork. Test at actual size. Print and view every variation at its intended size. Check counters, thin strokes and letter separation. Minimum production sizes remain pending testing. Balance partners. Match perceived visual weight, not bounding-box dimensions. Keep each original mark distinct. Label the Aesop and Slowear concepts as speculative. ← PREVIOUS Personality & voice NEXT → Typography Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "typography.html", "title": "Typography", "text": "Logo Typography Color VISUAL SYSTEM / TYPOGRAPHY Two voices. One hierarchy. Chubbo for expressive moments. National Park for clear information and the tagline. TYPOGRAPHY DISPLAY / CHUBBO A little at a time. Headlines, expressive statements, and course names. INFORMATION / NATIONAL PARK Take Your Sweet Time. Body copy, navigation, labels, descriptions, and the tagline. Try the type system Dessert is a reason to stay. Display 32–40 pt Section 24 / 29 pt Body 10.5 / 15 pt Caption 8.5 / 12 pt Proposed print settings. Use authentic font files; keep paragraphs left-aligned. For digital body copy, start at 16–18 px and test across screens. ← PREVIOUS Logo & variations NEXT → Color palette Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "review.html", "title": "Review checklist", "text": "Prompt library Review checklist Downloads WORKFLOW / REVIEW Review before release. Use this checklist to review identity, content and execution. Completion supports review; it does not replace owner approval. 0 OF 10 CHECKED Designer review → Technical review → Owner approval → Archive Reset checklist ↻ Checklist state is stored in this browser. Completion supports review; it does not record external owner approval. ← PREVIOUS AI prompt guide NEXT → Downloads Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "applications.html", "title": "Application library", "text": "Applications 05 / APPLICATION LIBRARY The same feeling. A different setting. Ten applications demonstrate what stays fixed—and what can adapt. WORKING STATUS Concepts, with clear release gates. Aesop and Slowear are speculative collaborations. Menu, social and motion specifications are proposed studies. Confirm technical production, partner artwork, product data and print proof before release. ← PREVIOUS Sensory & motion NEXT → AI prompt guide Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "patterns.html", "title": "Patterns & graphics", "text": "Patterns Grid & layout Image direction 03 / SECONDARY ASSETS A rhythm of our own. Extend the original contour through measured repetition, purposeful graphics, and a shared grid. Supporting graphics are separate from logo compositions. Use the original contour without distortion. Pattern 2 mirrors the supporting shape; never mirror the complete logo. ← PREVIOUS Color palette NEXT → Layout & grids Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "imagery.html", "title": "Image direction", "text": "Patterns Grid & layout Image direction VISUAL SYSTEM / IMAGERY Human scale. Real texture. A consistent direction for photography, illustration, and generated scenes. IMAGE DIRECTION Small servings. Intimate tables. Natural gestures. Terracotta, ceramics, glass and soft textiles, seen in warm light with gentle shadows. Avoid oversized portions, exaggerated melting, excessive greenery, ornate Italian clichés and generic luxury imagery. COMBINING ASSETS Give each element a role. Keep logos and essential copy clear of patterns and busy image details. Use one dominant image or statement per composition. Functional icons, illustration & generated imagery + ← → × — — — Icons Use simple arrows, progress and controls where they clarify interaction. Provide labels. Do not create new brand symbols. Illustration Photography leads. Use simple grid-aligned diagrams only to explain relationships or construction. Avoid mascots and unrelated decorative imagery. AI imagery Generate scenes from approved references. Apply authentic logos and type afterward. Review proportions, hands, glassware, materials and text. ← PREVIOUS Layout & grids NEXT → Sensory & motion Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "prompts.html", "title": "AI prompt guide", "text": "Prompt library Review checklist Downloads 06 / AI PROMPT GUIDE Human direction. Considered execution. The designer sets creative intent and approves the result. AI works within the established system. PERMANENT Keep the foundation. Purpose, audience, values, original logos, authentic typography, approved colors, warm voice, and asset fidelity. FLEXIBLE Adapt the application. Format, composition, scale, crop, placement, context, camera angle and project-specific production needs. Recommended tools & responsibilities + ChatGPT Briefs, copy alternatives and prompt structure. Review facts, meaning and voice. Image generation Exploratory scenes and visualizations. Apply original logos and authentic text in final artwork. Codex Responsive implementation and repeatable checks. Test functionality, layout and accessibility. Production tools Illustrator, InDesign and compositing for master assets and final typography. These are production tools, not generative models. Recommended workflow pending brand-owner approval. Record the tool/model, date, input assets, prompt, revisions and reviewer for each project. Build from the same foundation. REUSABLE PROMPTS Choose an application Include permanent brand foundation Copy complete prompt ↗ Structure: Brand foundation → Project brief → Visual direction → Deliverables → Review criteria. Each application card includes its context and example output. ENCOURAGE Warm. Clear. Real. Gentle invitations, small portions, believable textures, intimate settings, supplied artwork, and careful typography. “Try this next.” “A little more time together.” “Notice what changes.” REJECT Identity drift. Altered logos, simulated fonts, invented facts, unsupported claims, rushed language, unrelated symbols, decorative excess and false official partnerships. Avoid “hurry,” “ultimate luxury,” and exaggerated marketing superlatives. ← PREVIOUS Application library NEXT → Review checklist Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "layout.html", "title": "Layout & grids", "text": "Patterns Grid & layout Image direction VISUAL SYSTEM / LAYOUT Give expression room to breathe. Shared alignment, consistent margins, and a deliberate hierarchy connect every format. Show grid overlay + THE COMPOSITION PRINCIPLE One clear focal point. Let typography, imagery and supporting graphics work in a shared hierarchy. Print / 4 columns 7 × 8.5in. Inside 0.65in; outside 0.5in. Top 0.55in; bottom 0.65in. Gutter 0.15in. Desktop / 6 columns One shared container, up to 1,200px wide. Six equal columns with 24px gutters. Use 3 + 3 or 2 + 2 + 2 column groups. All page edges align. Mobile / 4 columns Stack content at 760px. Use 24px side margins and 16px gutters. Keep reading order, labels and controls intact. ← PREVIOUS Patterns & graphics NEXT → Image direction Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "brand.html", "title": "Brand overview", "text": "Foundations Voice & personality 01 / FOUNDATION Begin with the feeling. ’while turns dessert into a social pause. The identity is built to make that pause tangible. ON THIS PAGE The evening deserves a little more time. Three values. Everyday decisions. An after-dinner ritual ’while is a seated Italian gelato and wine experience for adults 35+, especially couples and close friends who want to continue the evening together. Three small pairings arrive one at a time: a bright opening, a creamier middle, and a lingering finish. Conversation fills the spaces between. POSITIONING A Coursed Ice Cream Bar A gelato-led tasting occasion between the restaurant and the bar. OUR PURPOSE To turn dessert into a social pause. Take Your Sweet Time. THE MANIFESTO The evening deserves a little more time. Time to notice a new flavor, linger over a conversation, and enjoy the company across the table. Some of the moments we want to keep happen after the plates have been cleared, when there is still more to say. ’while makes room for those moments. Italian gelato and wine come together in three thoughtful courses: a cool spoonful, a small sip, and a pause to see how the flavors unfold. We care about the craft behind each pairing and the comfort of feeling welcome. Come with curiosity. We’ll take care of the details. Take Your Sweet Time. VISION An evening ritual. Make an unhurried dessert experience a familiar way to continue the evening. MISSION One course at a time. Create thoughtful gelato and Italian wine pairings with room for conversation between them. AUDIENCE Time together. Adults 35+, couples and close friends who value considered food, comfort and approachable discovery. Three values. Everyday decisions. STRATEGIC PILLARS 01 Time Leave room for the evening to unfold. Sequential service. Spacious layouts. Gentle transitions. 02 Craft Choose every pairing and material with intention. Precise typography. Tactile materials. Careful finishing. 03 Comfort Make discovery easy and welcoming. Familiar language. Clear information. Intimate seating. ← PREVIOUS Overview NEXT → Personality & voice Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}, {"file": "index.html", "title": "Overview", "text": "’WHILE / BRAND GUIDELINES TIME. CRAFT. COMFORT. A little more time together. The identity behind an unhurried evening of Italian gelato, wine, and good company. Enter the guide ↗ THE ’WHILE EXPERIENCE Take Your Sweet Time. CONTENTS / 01—06 A shared language. Principles to begin with. Details to return to. 01 The Brand Purpose, people & voice ↗ 02 Visual Identity Logo, typography & color ↗ 03 Graphic Language Patterns, grids & imagery ↗ 04 The Experience Space, service & the senses ↗ 05 In Practice The identity in the world ↗ 06 AI & Assets Prompts, review & downloads ↗ Take Your Sweet Time. Brand concept & design · Paige Cui Brand assets ↗ BRAND GUIDELINES / 2026"}];